// `@env.set` writes an overlay this run owns, not the operating-system
// environment: `std::env::set_var` races every C library that reads the
// environment, and the runtime is multi-threaded. What the overlay guarantees is
// what this case asserts — a write reads back, and it reads back *over* whatever
// the process inherited.
do @env.set("RITE_CONFORMANCE_ONLY", "written")
^ ! @env.get("RITE_CONFORMANCE_ONLY")
